# Ollama Modelfile for a skycmd s1 model (llama.cpp architecture `modern-bert`, decision type
# `laya`). Put the GGUF next to this file, then:
#
#   curl -LO https://maxgfr.github.io/skycmd/models/s1-pico.gguf
#   ollama create skycmd-s1-pico -f Modelfile
#
# Status (see docs/compat.md): Ollama has no /v1/systemone endpoint and its engine does not run
# decision heads, so this file only registers the weights in an Ollama store. To answer
# requests, serve the same file with `skycmd serve` or llama.cpp `llama-server`.
# s2 GGUFs (`skycmd-s2`) are served only by the skycmd engine.
FROM ./s1-pico.gguf
